# UDAP metadata

The nx-fhir `auth-udap` feature makes this server publish signed UDAP metadata at `{baseURL}/.well-known/udap`. The metadata gives a client the endpoints of the authorization server of `app.auth.issuer`. That server registers clients, authorizes them, and issues tokens.

The metadata follows the HL7 FAST security IG (Security for Scalable Registration, Authentication, and Authorization), STU2 2.0.0.

The feature needs the `auth-resource` feature. It uses `app.auth.enabled`, the issuer, the `ssl-verify` key, and the shared classes of the `auth` package of that feature. When the server has no `auth-resource`, the install offers to install it first. In an interactive run, the install asks one question, and yes is the default. With yes, `auth-resource` installs first and asks its own questions. In a run that is not interactive, `auth-resource` installs with its defaults, and the install asks no question.

